hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"27604","Haddathana Yazid ibn Harun, he said: Akhbarana Abd Allah ibn Yazid ibn Miqsam, he said: My aunt Sarah bint Miqsam narrated to me from Maymunah bint Kardam, she said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, at Makkah while he was upon his she-camel, and I was with my father, and in the hand of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was a stick like the stick of schoolmasters, and I heard the Bedouins and the people saying: Al-tabtabiyyah. Then my father drew near to him and took hold of his foot, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, acknowledged him. She said: Among what I have not forgotten is the length of the index toe of his foot over the rest of his toes. She said: Then my father said to him: I witnessed the army of Ithran. She said: So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, recognized that army, and Tariq ibn al-Muraqqa' said: Who will give me a spear for its reward? He said: So I said: What is its reward? He said: I will marry him to the first daughter born to me. He said: So I gave him my spear, then I left him until a daughter was born to him and she matured, then I came to him and said to him: Prepare my wife for me, and he said: No, by Allah, I will not prepare her until you produce a dowry other than that, so I swore that I would not do so. Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: And how old is the woman? He said: She has seen grey hair. He said: So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to me: Leave her, there is no good in her for you. He said: That alarmed me, and I looked at him, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: You do not sin, nor does your companion sin. She said: Then my father said to him in that standing: I vowed to slaughter a number of sheep, I know it only as he said fifty sheep, upon Buwanah. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Is there anything of these idols upon it? He said: No. He said: Then fulfill for Allah what you vowed to Him. She said: So my father gathered them and began slaughtering them, and a sheep escaped from him, so he sought it saying: O Allah, fulfill my vow on my behalf, until he seized it and slaughtered it."
"27605","Haddathana Abd al-Samad, he said: Haddathana Abd Allah ibn Yazid ibn Dabbah al-Ta'ifi, he said: An aunt of mine called Sarah bint Miqsam narrated to me from her freedwoman Maymunah bint Kardam that she was with her father, and she mentioned that she saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, upon a she-camel with a stick in his hand, and she mentioned the hadith."
"27606","Haddathana Abu Ahmad, he said: Haddathana Abd Allah, meaning Ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Ya'la al-Ta'ifi, from Yazid ibn Miqsam, from his freedwoman Maymunah bint Kardam, she said: I was riding behind my father, and I heard him asking the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: O Messenger of Allah, I vowed to slaughter at Buwanah. So he said: Is there an idol or a false object of worship there? He said: No. He said: Fulfill your vow."
